                <pb facs="0495" n="447" xml:id="pg447"/>

                <head>253. Memorandum From Robert W. Komer of the National Security Council Staff to
                    the President’s Special Assistant for National Security Affairs (Bundy)<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d253-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1965-05-27">May 27, 1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">McGB—</p>
                <p> FYI, we may have a pro-Western coup in Ghana soon. Certain key military and
                    police figures have been planning one for some time, and Ghana’s deteriorating
                    economic condition may provide the spark.</p>
                <p>The plotters are keeping us briefed, and State thinks we’re more on the inside
                    than the British. While we’re not directly involved (I’m told), we and other
                    Western countries (including France) have been helping to set up the situation
                    by ignoring Nkrumah’s pleas for economic aid. The new OCAM (Francophone) group’s
                    refusal to attend any OAU meeting in Accra (because of Nkrumah’s plotting) will
                    further isolate him. All in all, looks good.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">RWK</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
